{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37144024",
      "title": "Returning Data When Leaving a Screen",
      "lectureOrder": 177,
      "videoOrder": 164,
      "sourceHash": "ced711fc12815142f837d2f662d9d4a5d80c12a9d178d4eb38f5ead8b90aab12",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "So we got this filters screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 5.88,
          "en": "where we can set our filters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.88,
          "end": 9.51,
          "en": "Now we wanna make sure that if this back button is pressed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.51,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "or also of course if the physical back button on the device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 17.4,
          "en": "might be pressed, we pass those selected filters back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 21.9,
          "en": "to the tabs screen where we then use them to, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.9,
          "end": 25.71,
          "en": "narrow down which meals will be shown if we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.71,
          "end": 27.753,
          "en": "select the hamburgers category.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "Now, therefore, we must find a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 33.93,
          "en": "of passing those variable values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.93,
          "end": 35.98,
          "en": "that are managed here in FiltersStart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.98,
          "end": 40.77,
          "en": "in the FiltersScreenState back to the taps screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.77,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "And for that of course, we need to find a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 46.65,
          "en": "of knowing when the user tapped the back button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "the physical one, or the one in the top left corner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 52.62,
          "en": "And this is another common requirement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.62,
          "end": 54.81,
          "en": "and therefore Flutter helps you with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.81,
          "end": 56.4,
          "en": "It gives you a special widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.4,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "which you can use here in your scaffold to wrap it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 60.87,
          "en": "around your body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.87,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "And therefore that's what I'll do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "I'll wrap a widget around my column here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 67.05,
          "en": "And the widget I will wrap",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 71.842,
          "en": "around it is the WillPopScope widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.842,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "WillPopScope is a utility widget that, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 79.68,
          "en": "essentially wraps the entire content of this screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.68,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "And WillPopScope allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 87.98,
          "en": "and actually wants you to set a onWillPop parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 91.89,
          "en": "And onWillPop actually wants a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.89,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "that returns a future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 96.9,
          "en": "And you might recall I mentioned futures earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.9,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "Futures are these objects which eventually resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 101.82,
          "en": "to other values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.82,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "Values which are not there yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.43,
          "en": "So a function that returns such a future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.43,
          "end": 110.25,
          "en": "And that function will be invoked by Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.25,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "whenever the user tries to leave this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 116.05,
          "en": "So here we can pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 119.97,
          "en": "and this function receives no arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.97,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "but in this function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 126.74,
          "en": "we can now manually call Navigator.of.context.pop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 133.05,
          "en": "And the advantage of doing so is that pop actually allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.05,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "to pass some data along with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "Some data, which will then be available in the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.06,
          "en": "where we navigated to this screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 142.803,
          "en": "so to the filters screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "Well, in that place is our tabs screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "There, it's in this setScreen method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 150.93,
          "en": "where we in the end navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.93,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "to the filters screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 155.43,
          "en": "So therefore it will be here where we will get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 158.19,
          "en": "to the data returned with help of pop from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.19,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "inside this filters screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 163.5,
          "en": "Now here you can return any kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.5,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "and what I will return here will be a map where I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 169.23,
          "en": "to have different keys for my different filters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.23,
          "end": 171.45,
          "en": "and then true or false, depending on whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.45,
          "end": 173.19299999999998,
          "en": "that filter has been set or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.39,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "Now, for that to standardize those keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 179.79,
          "en": "I'll actually add a enum in this FiltersStart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.79,
          "end": 183,
          "en": "at the very top of the file, which I'll name Filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "And here I'll add some unique identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 188.01,
          "en": "for all these filters that we can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.01,
          "end": 191.283,
          "en": "So here I'll go for glutenFree, lactoseFree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 193.92,
          "en": "vegetarian,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 195.093,
          "en": "and vegan,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.28,
          "end": 199.59,
          "en": "so that we have these clearly defined keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.59,
          "end": 201.75,
          "en": "And these should be my keys in this map,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.75,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "which I wanna return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.863,
          "en": "So my map here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 208.8,
          "en": "which I'm returning in pop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.8,
          "end": 212.94299999999998,
          "en": "will have those different enum values as keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.07999999999998,
          "end": 218.01,
          "en": "So Filter.glutenFree as a key, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.01,
          "end": 220.71,
          "en": "and then as a value separated by a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.71,
          "end": 224.46,
          "en": "as you learned, the currently stored value for that filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.46,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "which for this glutenFreeFilter would be stored in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "_glutenFreeFilterSet variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 233.403,
          "en": "So that's the value I wanna set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.57,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "And I'll now repeat this for all my other filters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 243.393,
          "en": "So for lactoseFree, for vegetarian,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.58,
          "end": 249.813,
          "en": "and for vegan like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.22,
          "end": 254.37,
          "en": "And therefore this map here will be in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.37,
          "end": 257.1,
          "en": "what will be returned by this Filters screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 258,
          "en": "when it's popped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 259.98,
          "en": "So when the back button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.98,
          "end": 262.68,
          "en": "And we will then be able to access this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.68,
          "end": 265.11,
          "en": "this map here from inside the tabs screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.11,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "because data is where we navigated to this filters screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "Now we're not entirely done yet though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.84,
          "end": 273.3,
          "en": "Instead here in this WillPopScope widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "in this function here, we have to return true or false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 279.9,
          "en": "to in the end confirm whether we want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.9,
          "end": 281.97,
          "en": "to navigate back or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.97,
          "end": 284.46,
          "en": "And since we are navigating back manually here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.46,
          "end": 286.11,
          "en": "we should indeed return false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 288.45,
          "en": "so that we're not popping twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.45,
          "end": 291.21,
          "en": "If you would not be popping manually here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.21,
          "end": 294.69,
          "en": "but doing anything else, like saving data to some database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 294.69,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "it would make sense to return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "instead, if you wanted to allow the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 301.35,
          "en": "to leave the screen, here, we'll return false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.35,
          "end": 304.08,
          "en": "Since we already have our leave screen logic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.08,
          "end": 305.97,
          "en": "and we don't wanna pop twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.97,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "because that would essentially mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 310.023,
          "en": "that we would probably close our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 312.15,
          "en": "So here we return false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 312.15,
          "end": 315.09,
          "en": "but here we pop manually, essentially leaving the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 317.76,
          "en": "with this data being passed back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 317.76,
          "end": 319.5,
          "en": "And now we just have to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.5,
          "end": 322.38,
          "en": "that onWillPop actually wants a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 322.38,
          "end": 323.91,
          "en": "that returns a future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 323.91,
          "end": 326.07,
          "en": "which eventually yields a Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "instead of getting a Boolean right away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 330.81,
          "en": "And therefore, to make sure that this is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.81,
          "end": 333.42,
          "en": "we should add the async keyword here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.42,
          "end": 335.31,
          "en": "between this empty parameter list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 335.31,
          "end": 337.47,
          "en": "and the opening curly brace.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 337.47,
          "end": 339.42,
          "en": "Because by adding async here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 339.42,
          "end": 342.3,
          "en": "you can not only use the await keyword as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 342.3,
          "end": 344.28,
          "en": "before in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 344.28,
          "end": 347.76,
          "en": "but instead you will also automatically wrap the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 347.76,
          "end": 350.7,
          "en": "returned here into such a future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 350.7,
          "end": 353.37,
          "en": "So that's a convenient way of creating a future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 353.37,
          "end": 356.01,
          "en": "that will be returned by your function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 356.01,
          "end": 359.55,
          "en": "So by adding async here, this function will return a future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 359.55,
          "end": 363.75,
          "en": "that will then eventually resolve to this false value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 363.75,
          "end": 367.8,
          "en": "And with that, we have control over this going back process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 367.8,
          "end": 370.44,
          "en": "and we pop manually with our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 370.44,
          "end": 373.74,
          "en": "Now we just need to read that data in that place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 373.74,
          "end": 376.8,
          "en": "where we navigate it to the FiltersScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
